    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "Well, on the last point, I don't think there's any ambiguity left. I think there's got to be consensus in the country of not unanimity that none of this would have happened without Donald Trump. Is there anybody who really thinks that if Donald Trump had just conceded the election and said this was over, he was disappointed that 60-plus courts had rejected every claim of electoral fraud and corruption. He was disappointed that the electoral college went 306 to 232 for Biden and the popular vote went seven million votes for Biden. He disagrees with it. He's still imagined theoretically there's some fraud out there that have been proven. But he was going to go home and do the right thing like every other president in American history. Does anybody think that we would have suffered these repeated efforts at a political coup and then a violent insurrection? I mean, it was defies, you know, any reason, it all came from him. And I think we've been able to demonstrate every element of the successive attempts to overthrow the 2020 presidential election result and can have Trump seize the presidency. That story is clear for people. We're going to fill in some more details in our final hearing, but essentially",
