    "turn_text": "The religious cult aspect of it. I think any religious cult is like that. There's a mystery to it. I always go back to Thomas Paine, the original principles upon which America resisted to remember them rightly as repossessing them. We don't seem to be possessing the founding fathers put forth. The other thing that Paine said that always comes back to mind is I become irritated that the attempt to govern mankind by force and fraud as if we're all naves and fools. And that always reminds me of Donald Trump.",
