    "turn_text": "One of the biggest problems I have with that is our my professions, um, complicity. in it. And I have, you know, the book that I just wrote, Free the Press. And by the way, thank you. And I'm going to bring that up. You were on the floor of the house trying to speak to a reporter's right to keep a confidential source. And hopefully that bill will pass this time. But our My profession has been stripped since Ronald Reagan. The wheels have come off. The guidelines are gone. There's no restraint. So you've had smaller and smaller numbers of companies own more and more of what's going on. There's little diversity in reporting. And it was Ben Bagdicki. And at the Washington Post has said, if you want to have true diversity in government or true diversity in our country represented, you have to have diversity of ownership. in reporting. And when I first got into this business, 80% of what you see reader here was owned by maybe 20 companies. Today, six companies own 90% of what you see reader here. And I'm concerned that we are allowing the autocrats to overcome democracy because we're more interested in clickbait and profit than doing our job. How do you deal with that?",
